Runtime text retained-host subpixel bin precision validation
Date: 2026-07-04
Scope: editor retained-host small Latin labels from the user crop: `editor base.zui` and `folder-open.svg`.

Problem addressed:
- DengXian/等线 was selected, but per-character horizontal placement still showed visible left/right unevenness.
- The retained-host text painter quantized pen-origin phase into 4 bins before rasterization, leaving up to 0.125px origin error and causing near-right phases such as 20.90 to roll to the next pixel cell.

Implementation evidence:
- `zircon_editor/src/ui/retained_host/host_contract/paint_text/draw/glyphs.rs`
  - `TEXT_RASTER_SUPERSAMPLE` is now 8.0 for fallback alpha-mask rasterization.
  - `RETAINED_TEXT_SUBPIXEL_BINS` is now 8, producing 0 / .125 / .25 / .375 / .5 / .625 / .75 / .875 phases.
- `zircon_editor/src/ui/retained_host/host_contract/paint_text/draw/glyphs/tests.rs`
  - `retained_glyph_placement_uses_eight_phase_bins_for_editor_labels` locks the precision contract.
  - `retained_glyph_placement_uses_nearest_subpixel_bin_without_left_bias` now asserts 20.90 remains pixel 20 with phase .875 and only 20.95 rolls to the next pixel.

Checks run:
- `rustfmt --edition 2021 --check zircon_editor/src/ui/retained_host/host_contract/paint_text/draw/glyphs.rs zircon_editor/src/ui/retained_host/host_contract/paint_text/draw/glyphs/tests.rs` passed.

Deferred checks:
- Focused Cargo was not started because external cargo/rustc lanes were active.

